<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaCl                                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> FeCl<sub>2</sub> solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=187">187</a>)                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace element solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=187">187</a>)           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;900.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components and adjust pH to 7.0.  Distribute the medium into tubes or bottles under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers, and autoclave.  After cooling, add per liter (final) the following solutions from sterile anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):    <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Substrate solution (see below)                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;100.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 3% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                     </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Readjust pH of the medium to 7.0, if necessary. <br>
<I>Substrate solution:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> L-Sodium lactate                                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;12.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;12.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;100.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml        </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
